---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { appConfig } from "../app-config";

const effective = "May 19, 2026";
const updated = "May 19, 2026";

const toc = [
  { id: "agreement", label: "Agreement" },
  { id: "service", label: "The service" },
  { id: "eligibility", label: "Eligibility" },
  { id: "account", label: "Your account" },
  { id: "acceptable-use", label: "Acceptable use" },
  { id: "subscriptions", label: "Subscriptions & payments" },
  { id: "refunds", label: "Refunds" },
  { id: "ip", label: "Intellectual property" },
  { id: "feedback", label: "Feedback" },
  { id: "religious", label: "Religious content" },
  { id: "store-terms", label: "App store terms" },
  { id: "third-party", label: "Third-party services" },
  { id: "disclaimers", label: "Disclaimers" },
  { id: "liability", label: "Limitation of liability" },
  { id: "indemnity", label: "Indemnification" },
  { id: "termination", label: "Termination" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes to terms" },
  { id: "law", label: "Governing law" },
  { id: "disputes", label: "Disputes" },
  { id: "misc", label: "Miscellaneous" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact" },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of service — Barakah"
  description="The terms that govern your use of the Barakah app and website. Read carefully — they set the expectations between you and us."
  heading="Terms of service"
  eyebrow="Legal · Terms"
  effective={effective}
  updated={updated}
  toc={toc}
>
  <p class="lead">
    Bismillah. Thank you for choosing Barakah. These terms describe the relationship between you
    and {appConfig.brand.legalName} when you use Barakah. By using the service, you agree to be
    bound by them.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>In plain words:</strong> Barakah helps you put your phone down during salah. We
      respect your trust, do not sell your data, and ask in return that you use the app honestly,
      pay for paid features fairly, and respect the work that goes into it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section id="agreement">
    <h2 data-index="01">Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      By installing, accessing, or using Barakah (the “service”), you agree to these terms and to
      our <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not use the service.
      The service is provided by {appConfig.brand.legalName} (“we”, “us”, “our”).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="service">
    <h2 data-index="02">The service</h2>
    <p>
      Barakah is a quiet companion for salah. It helps you put aside the apps you choose during the
      five daily prayers — fajr, dhuhr, asr, maghrib, and isha — so you can show up, not scroll.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>You choose which apps to lock and during which prayer windows.</li>
      <li>Prayer windows are calculated using standard astronomical methods for your location.</li>
      <li>We do not read the contents of locked apps or your messages.</li>
      <li>
        Features and methods may evolve. We will not silently weaken the privacy guarantees of the
        service.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="eligibility">
    <h2 data-index="03">Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 13 years old (or the minimum digital-consent age in your jurisdiction)
      to use Barakah. If you are under the age of majority where you live, you may only use the
      service with the involvement of a parent or guardian who accepts these terms on your behalf.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="account">
    <h2 data-index="04">Your account</h2>
    <p>
      Some features require an account. You agree to provide accurate information and to keep your
      credentials safe. You are responsible for activity that happens under your account. Tell us
      promptly at
      <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.contact.email}`}>{appConfig.contact.email}</a>
      if you suspect unauthorized access.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="acceptable-use">
    <h2 data-index="05">Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Reverse engineer, decompile, or attempt to extract the source code of the service.</li>
      <li>Resell, sublicense, or redistribute the service without our written permission.</li>
      <li>Use the service to harass, deceive, defraud, or harm others.</li>
      <li>Use the service to spread content that mocks or misrepresents Islam or any community.</li>
      <li>Interfere with the integrity or performance of the service or its infrastructure.</li>
      <li>Use automated means (scrapers, bots) to access the service without our written consent.</li>
      <li>Violate any applicable law, including export controls and sanctions.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="subscriptions">
    <h2 data-index="06">Subscriptions and payments</h2>
    <p>
      Paid plans, including lifetime early access, are billed via our payment processor. Prices are
      shown in the currency stated at checkout. Applicable taxes are charged where required.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Lifetime early access</strong> is a one-time purchase that grants access to the
        current app and feature set for the supported lifetime of the product. It is not a perpetual
        promise of every future feature.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Subscriptions</strong>, where offered, renew automatically until canceled. You can
        manage renewal in the App Store or Play Store where the subscription was purchased.
      </li>
      <li>We may change pricing for future purchases; existing lifetime plans are not re-billed.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="refunds">
    <h2 data-index="07">Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      For purchases made through the Apple App Store or Google Play Store, refunds are handled by
      those stores under their respective policies. For purchases made directly from us, refund
      requests within 14 days of purchase will be honored where required by law or where you have
      not made substantial use of the service. Email
      <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.contact.email}`}>{appConfig.contact.email}</a>
      to start a refund request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="ip">
    <h2 data-index="08">Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Barakah name, logo, source code, designs, copy, and content are owned by us or our
      licensors and are protected by applicable law. We grant you a limited, non-exclusive,
      non-transferable, revocable license to use the service for personal, non-commercial purposes,
      subject to these terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="feedback">
    <h2 data-index="09">Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you send us ideas, suggestions, or feedback, you grant us a worldwide, royalty-free,
      perpetual license to use them to improve the service without obligation to you. We will not
      attribute feedback to you publicly without your permission.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="religious">
    <h2 data-index="10">Religious content</h2>
    <p>
      Barakah surfaces prayer times and Islamic concepts. We aim for accuracy and respect the
      traditions and scholarship of the Muslim ummah. However, we do not issue fatwa, and the app
      is not a substitute for guidance from a qualified scholar.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prayer time calculations differ by method (ISNA, MWL, Umm al-Qura, Egyptian, Karachi, and
      others). Times shown are estimates based on your device location and the method you choose;
      please verify with your local masjid where precision is critical.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="store-terms">
    <h2 data-index="11">App store terms</h2>
    <p>
      If you obtained Barakah from the Apple App Store, you acknowledge that these terms are between
      you and us — not Apple — and that Apple has no obligation to provide support for the app.
      Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these terms and may enforce them.
      Equivalent terms apply to the Google Play Store and Google.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-party">
    <h2 data-index="12">Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Barakah relies on third-party services for hosting, analytics, payments, and notifications.
      Their use is governed by their own terms and privacy policies. We choose them with care but
      are not responsible for their content or practices.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="disclaimers">
    <h2 data-index="13">Disclaimers</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided “as is” and “as available” without warranties of any kind, express or
      implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
      non-infringement, to the maximum extent permitted by law. We do not warrant that the service
      will be uninterrupted, error-free, or perfectly accurate at all times.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability">
    <h2 data-index="14">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, {appConfig.brand.legalName} and its officers,
      employees, and agents will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential,
      exemplary, or punitive damages, or any loss of profits, revenue, data, or goodwill, arising
      out of or in connection with your use of the service. Our total aggregate liability for any
      claim arising out of or relating to the service will not exceed the greater of (a) the amount
      you paid us in the 12 months preceding the claim, or (b) USD 50.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="indemnity">
    <h2 data-index="15">Indemnification</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to indemnify and hold us harmless from any claim, loss, liability, or expense
      (including reasonable attorney fees) arising from your misuse of the service, your violation
      of these terms, or your infringement of any third-party right.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="termination">
    <h2 data-index="16">Termination</h2>
    <p>
      You may stop using the service at any time. We may suspend or terminate access if you violate
      these terms or use the service in a way that risks harm to others or to the service.
      Provisions that by their nature should survive termination — including intellectual property,
      disclaimers, liability limits, and dispute resolution — will survive.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2 data-index="17">Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms as the service evolves. If changes are material, we will give you
      reasonable notice in-app or by email. Continued use after changes take effect means you
      accept the updated terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="law">
    <h2 data-index="18">Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws applicable to {appConfig.brand.legalName}, without
      regard to conflict-of-law principles. Where local consumer-protection law gives you stronger
      rights, those rights are not diminished by this section.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="disputes">
    <h2 data-index="19">Disputes</h2>
    <p>
      Before filing a formal claim, please contact us at
      <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.contact.email}`}>{appConfig.contact.email}</a>
      so we have a chance to resolve the matter directly. If a dispute cannot be resolved
      informally within 60 days, the parties may pursue available remedies in a court of competent
      jurisdiction or, where applicable, binding arbitration on an individual basis.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="misc">
    <h2 data-index="20">Miscellaneous</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Entire agreement.</strong> These terms and the privacy policy are the entire
        agreement between you and us regarding the service.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Severability.</strong> If any provision is held unenforceable, the remaining
        provisions remain in effect.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No waiver.</strong> Our failure to enforce any right is not a waiver of that right.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Assignment.</strong> You may not assign these terms without our consent; we may
        assign them as part of a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Notices.</strong> We may give notice by in-app message or by email.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2 data-index="21">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? Reach us at
      <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.contact.email}`}>{appConfig.contact.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <address>
      {appConfig.brand.legalName}<br />
      Attn: Legal<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.contact.email}`}>{appConfig.contact.email}</a>
    </address>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <p>
    JazakAllah khair for using Barakah. May your salah be a place of peace, and may He grant you
    barakah in your time, ameen.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
